API design for the Session module of a coaching platform — versioned REST contract, dual validation (schema + business).

1. Endpoint contract

- `GET /api/session` — liste paginée (page, par-page plafonné) ;
- `GET /api/session/{id}` — fiche complète ;
- `POST /api/session` — création (201, Location) ;
- `PATCH /api/session/{id}` — mise à jour partielle ;
- `DELETE /api/session/{id}` — suppression (204).

2. Implementation

CRUD API route for Session (paginated list + validated creation) — `app/api/session/route.ts` :
```ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { z } from "zod";
import { prisma } from "@/lib/prisma";
import { requireUser } from "@/lib/security/authenticated-request";

const SchemaCreation = z.object({ /* champs métier */ });

export async function GET(request: NextRequest) {
  await requireUser(request);
  const page = Number(new URL(request.url).searchParams.get("page") ?? 1);
  const items = await prisma.session.findMany({ orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" }, take: 20, skip: (page - 1) * 20 });
  return NextResponse.json({ items });
}

export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  const utilisateur = await requireUser(request);
  const body = SchemaCreation.parse(await request.json());
  const cree = await prisma.session.create({ data: { ...body, ownerId: utilisateur.uid } });
  return NextResponse.json(cree, { status: 201 });
}
```

3. Normalized errors

- 400 — invalid body (failing field detail in the response)
- 401 — missing or expired session
- 404 — unknown resource (no information leak)
- 429 — rate limited (retry-after header)
- 500 — internal failure (trace id in logs only)

