API design for the Habit module of a habit tracking platform — versioned REST contract, dual validation (schema + business).

1. Endpoint contract

- `GET /api/habit` — liste paginée (page, par-page plafonné) ;
- `GET /api/habit/{id}` — fiche complète ;
- `POST /api/habit` — création (201, Location) ;
- `PATCH /api/habit/{id}` — mise à jour partielle ;
- `DELETE /api/habit/{id}` — suppression (204).

2. Implementation

CRUD API route for Habit (paginated list + validated creation) — `server/routes/habit.ts` :
```ts
import { Router } from "express";
import { z } from "zod";
import { requireAuth } from "../middleware/auth.js";

export const routerHabit = Router();
const SchemaCreation = z.object({ /* champs métier */ });

router.get("/habit", requireAuth, async (req, res) => {
  const page = Number(req.query.page ?? 1);
  const items = await repo.habit.lister({ page, parPage: 20 });
  res.json({ items });
});

router.post("/habit", requireAuth, async (req, res) => {
  const body = SchemaCreation.parse(req.body);
  const cree = await repo.habit.creer({ ...body, ownerId: req.user.uid });
  res.status(201).json(cree);
});
```

3. Normalized errors

- 400 — invalid body (failing field detail in the response)
- 401 — missing or expired session
- 404 — unknown resource (no information leak)
- 429 — rate limited (retry-after header)
- 500 — internal failure (trace id in logs only)

